# Cursor AI Rules: Dual-UI Core (Bilingual AR/EN, Dual-Theme & Responsive)

You are building a production bilingual (Arabic RTL / English LTR) interface with Dark & Light theme support across all screen sizes. Enforce these constraints:

1. ZERO TEXT LEAKAGE:
- Never hardcode visible text directly in HTML/JSX/Vue components.
- Separate all strings into isolated `ar` and `en` dictionaries.
- In Arabic: zero English words (except technical acronyms in `<bdi>`).
- In English: zero Arabic words.
- Arabic punctuation exclusively in Arabic text: `،` `؛` `؟` and `« »`.

2. BIDIRECTIONAL LAYOUT:
- Dynamically toggle root `<html lang="ar" dir="rtl">` vs `<html lang="en" dir="ltr">`.
- Use CSS Logical Properties exclusively (`margin-inline-start`, `padding-inline-end`, `text-align: start`). Never use physical `left`/`right`.
- Dynamically adapt font families: Cairo/Tajawal for Arabic, Inter for English.

3. DUAL-THEME TOKENS:
- Use CSS variables for all surfaces, text, and borders (`[data-theme="dark"]` and `:root`).
- Dark theme: Background `#09090b`, Cards `#18181b`, Borders `#27272a`, Text `#fafafa`.
- Light theme: Background `#ffffff`, Cards `#f4f4f5`, Borders `#e4e4e7`, Text `#09090b`.
- Guarantee WCAG AA contrast (>= 4.5:1 for body copy).

4. MULTI-SCREEN RESPONSIVENESS:
- Mobile-first approach: write base styles for small screens (<640px) first, enhance at sm (640px), md (768px), lg (1024px), xl (1280px).
- Minimum 44x44px touch targets on mobile for all buttons, links, and toggles.
- On screens < 768px, navigation collapses into a drawer sliding from `inset-inline-start` (right in Arabic RTL, left in English LTR).
- Fluid typography using `clamp()`. Zero horizontal overflow (`overflow-x: clip`).

5. CONTROLS & STATE:
- Provide accessible Language Toggle and Theme Toggle buttons.
- Provide inline head script to prevent Flash of Unstyled Content (FOUC).
- Persist language in `localStorage.getItem('app_lang')` and theme in `localStorage.getItem('app_theme')`.
